abiword: configure.ac without autoconf-archive and the old libgcrypt.m4.

The release tag has no generated configure; autogen.sh runs autoreconf, and
that failed ("configure.ac:70: error: possibly undefined macro:
AC_MSG_ERROR"): the --with-sanitizer block uses AX_CHECK_COMPILE_FLAG and
AX_APPEND_COMPILE_FLAGS from autoconf-archive, which the build machine does
not have, and the unexpanded macro's AC_MSG_ERROR argument is what autoconf
reported (at a wrong line). The block (a debugging option) now adds the
flags without checking them first. AX_CXX_COMPILE_STDCXX_11 (also
autoconf-archive, left unexpanded it broke configure: "syntax error near
unexpected token `noext,mandatory'") is replaced by what it did, -std=gnu++11
in CXXFLAGS: the code does not build as C++17, GCC 12's default (dynamic
exception specifications, std::pointer_to_unary_function). The bundled libgcrypt.m4 is deleted as
Debian does (drop-outdated-libgcrypt.m4.diff): an outdated copy of macros
autoreconf otherwise takes over the installed ones.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

diff -ruN abia/configure.ac abib/configure.ac
--- abia/configure.ac	2026-02-18 12:16:18.000000000 +0900
+++ abib/configure.ac	2026-11-25 18:06:50.010822675 +0900
@@ -131,7 +131,9 @@
 
 AC_PROG_CC
 AC_PROG_CXX
-AX_CXX_COMPILE_STDCXX_11(noext,mandatory)
+dnl AX_CXX_COMPILE_STDCXX_11(noext,mandatory) is autoconf-archive: the same
+dnl effect without it. The code is C++11 (it does not build as C++17).
+CXXFLAGS="$CXXFLAGS -std=gnu++11"
 #AC_PROG_OBJC
 AC_PROG_INSTALL
 # For libtool 1.5.x compatability (AC_PROG_LIBTOOL is deprecated version of LT_INIT)
@@ -626,14 +628,8 @@
             [with_sanitizer=$withval],
             [with_sanitizer=no])
 AS_IF([test "x$with_sanitizer" != "xno"],[
-	AX_CHECK_COMPILE_FLAG([-fsanitize=$withval],
-	                      [CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -fsanitize=$withval"
-			       CXXFLAGS="$CXXFLAGS -fsanitize=$withval"],
-	                      [AC_MSG_ERROR([-fsanitize=$withval is not supported])])
-        AX_APPEND_COMPILE_FLAGS([-fno-omit-frame-pointer])
-        AC_LANG_PUSH(C++)
-        AX_APPEND_COMPILE_FLAGS([-fno-omit-frame-pointer])
-        AC_LANG_POP
+	CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -fsanitize=$with_sanitizer -fno-omit-frame-pointer"
+	CXXFLAGS="$CXXFLAGS -fsanitize=$with_sanitizer -fno-omit-frame-pointer"
 ])
 
 #
